  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B017",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B024",
    "B031"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration has changed from B024 to B017. Optical lattice clocks rest upon a clean physical mechanism: magic-wavelength confinement suppresses a central perturbation while permitting precise interrogation of many atoms. The result is not only an elegant proposal but a mature, independently realized measurement regime with wide physical use. Katori and Ye provide a compact and plausible attribution to the originating architecture and its foundational realization. This is an unusually strong union of an intelligible physical idea, experimental verification, and durable capability.",
    "case_against": "The citation must remain limited to invention and realization of optical lattice clocks, rather than assign all later performance advances or any future redefinition of the second to two people. Historical review is still needed to distinguish the indispensable original contributions of Katori and Ye from subsequent technical developments.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that repeated independent realization makes optical lattice clocks a durable physical capability, while cautioning that the original invention must be distinguished from later advances.",
        "response": "I agree, and this distinction is decisive in my reassessment. B017 need not rely on prospective metrological adoption: the independently reproduced architecture and its demonstrated precision already establish maturity. A narrowly drawn invention-and-realization citation also avoids converting a collective later development into an overbroad individual claim."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth favors B024 for revealing fundamental quantum phase, but recognizes that the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase have distinct histories and may be difficult to unite in one citation.",
        "response": "I retain deep respect for B024 and regard observable quantum phase as one of the most fruitful ideas in modern physics. Yet the unresolved problem is structural, not merely verbal: the two effects are distinct discoveries with different priority histories. B017 now seems the more defensible final configuration because its physical mechanism, achievement boundary, and two-person credit can be stated together without that historical compression."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll emphasizes the magic-wavelength concept, broad reproducibility, and the coherent attribution of Katori and Ye, while separating those contributions from later optical-clock development.",
        "response": "I concur. From the perspective of statistical physics, the important virtue is that the essential mechanism is transparent and robust, rather than an accidental feature of one exceptional apparatus. The remaining attribution work should test the historical roles carefully, but the proposed two names correspond to a sufficiently delimited conceptual and experimental core."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record confirms that Katori's concept and Ye's foundational experimental contributions are the appropriate limited attribution relative to other early optical-clock contributors.",
      "Whether B024 can ultimately be reformulated around a single sufficiently bounded achievement without obscuring the separate histories of the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "My Gothenburg institutional environment is linked to the Chalmers environment of Göran Johansson and Eva Olsson, but no specific collaboration or connection to the B017 laureates is supplied. No conflict with the proposed configuration is apparent."
  }
}
